### Stream text responses with streamText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/providers/03-observability/maxim.mdx

Streams text chunks from a wrapped Maxim model using streamText and iterates over textStream.

```javascript
import { streamText } from 'ai';

const { textStream } = await streamText({
  model: model,
  prompt: 'Write a short story about space exploration',
  system: 'You are a creative writer',
});

for await (const textPart of textStream) {
  process.stdout.write(textPart);
}
```

--------------------------------

### Stream text with streamText and iterate chunks

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/03-ai-sdk-core/05-generating-text.mdx

Use streamText to stream text responses from an LLM and consume chunks asynchronously using result.textStream.

```typescript
import { streamText } from 'ai';
__PROVIDER_IMPORT__;

const result = streamText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  prompt: 'Invent a new holiday and describe its traditions.',
});

// example: use textStream as an async iterable
for await (const textPart of result.textStream) {
  console.log(textPart);
}
```

--------------------------------

### Stream text generation with streamText

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/02-foundations/05-streaming.mdx

Stream text generation from a language model and iterate over the text chunks as they arrive using an async iterable stream.

```ts
import { streamText } from 'ai';
__PROVIDER_IMPORT__;

const { textStream } = streamText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  prompt: 'Write a poem about embedding models.',
});

for await (const textPart of textStream) {
  console.log(textPart);
}
```

--------------------------------

### streamText(options)

Source: https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/content/docs/07-reference/01-ai-sdk-core/02-stream-text.mdx

Streams text generation from a language model and exposes event hooks such as onLanguageModelCallEnd to monitor performance, tokens, and response details.

```APIDOC
### Function
`streamText(options)`

### Parameters

- **onLanguageModelCallEnd** (`(event: LanguageModelCallEndEvent) => PromiseLike<void> | void`, optional) - Callback called after the model response has been normalized and parsed, but before any client-side tool execution begins. Errors thrown in this callback are silently caught and do not break the generation flow.

#### `LanguageModelCallEndEvent` Properties

- **callId** (`string`) - Unique identifier for the generation call.
- **provider** (`string`) - The provider identifier for this model call.
- **modelId** (`string`) - The provider-returned model identifier for this model call.
- **finishReason** (`FinishReason`) - The unified reason why the model call finished.
- **usage** (`LanguageModelUsage`) - Token usage reported by the model call.
- **content** (`ReadonlyArray<ContentPart<TOOLS>>`) - The content parts produced by the model call (text, reasoning, files, tool calls, etc.).
- **responseId** (`string`) - The provider-returned response ID for this model call.
- **providerMetadata** (`ProviderMetadata | undefined`) - Provider-specific metadata for this model call, when returned by the provider.
- **performance** (`LanguageModelCallPerformance`) - Performance metrics for the model call.
  - **responseTimeMs** (`number`) - Time spent waiting for the language model response in milliseconds.
  - **effectiveOutputTokensPerSecond** (`number`) - Effective number of output tokens per second over the full language model response.
  - **outputTokensPerSecond** (`number | undefined`) - Number of output tokens per second after the first generated output chunk was received. Only available for streaming model calls.
  - **inputTokensPerSecond** (`number | undefined`) - Number of input tokens processed per second before the first generated output chunk was received. Only available for streaming model calls.
  - **effectiveTotalTokensPerSecond** (`number`) - Effective number of input and output tokens per second over the full language model response.
  - **timeToFirstOutputMs** (`number | undefined`) - Time until the first generated output chunk was received in milliseconds. Only available for streaming model calls.
  - **timeBetweenOutputChunksMs** (`OutputChunkTimingStats | undefined`) - Timing statistics between output chunks.
```

